---
import StaticPage from '@/layouts/StaticPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/config/site';
---

<StaticPage
  eyebrow="Legal"
  h1="Terms & Conditions"
  lead="The simple rules for using MyJSONPal. By using the site, you agree to these terms."
  metaTitle="Terms & Conditions | MyJSONPal"
  metaDescription="Read the terms and conditions for using MyJSONPal — a free, privacy-first, in-browser JSON formatter and converter. Last updated August 2026."
  keywords={['terms and conditions', 'terms of service', 'myjsonpal terms', 'json tool terms']}
  path="/terms/"
  updated="August 1, 2026"
>
  <h2 id="acceptance">Acceptance of terms</h2>
  <p>
    By accessing or using MyJSONPal ("the Site", "we", "us"), you agree to be bound by these
    Terms & Conditions and all applicable laws and regulations. If you do not agree with any
    part of these terms, please do not use the Site.
  </p>

  <h2 id="service-description">Description of service</h2>
  <p>
    The Site provides free, browser-based tools for formatting, validating, repairing,
    minifying, and converting JSON and other data formats. All processing happens locally in
    your browser. We do not store, transmit, or otherwise process the data you enter on any of
    our servers.
  </p>

  <h2 id="acceptable-use">Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to misuse the Site, including by:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Attempting to disrupt, overload, or impair the Site's infrastructure.</li>
    <li>
      Using the Site to process or distribute illegal content, malware, or any material that
      violates applicable law.
    </li>
    <li>
      Attempting to reverse engineer, scrape, or otherwise circumvent any part of the Site.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="no-warranty">No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    The Site and its tools are provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any
    kind, whether express or implied, including implied warranties of merchantability, fitness
    for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. We do not warrant that the tools will be
    uninterrupted, error-free, or that outputs will be free of defects.
  </p>

  <h2 id="limitation-of-liability">Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, MyJSONPal and its operator shall not be liable
    for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or any loss of
    profits or data, arising out of or related to your use of the Site, even if advised of the
    possibility of such damages.
  </p>

  <h2 id="intellectual-property">Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The Site's design, branding, and code are owned by MyJSONPal unless otherwise credited.
    Your data and its output remain yours — we never claim ownership of the content you process.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes-to-terms">Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may revise these terms from time to time. Updated terms will be posted on this page with
    a revised "Last updated" date. Continued use of the Site after changes constitutes
    acceptance of the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="governing-law">Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by applicable local laws. Any disputes arising from the use of the
    Site shall be resolved in the appropriate courts of that jurisdiction.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or use
    our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</StaticPage>
